{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1554682-radiant-physicians-an-ancient-medical-legacy","id":1554682,"title":"Radiant Physicians - an ancient medical Legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-26T02:46:25-07:00","id":1554682,"title":"Radiant Physicians - an ancient medical Legacy","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Radiant Physicians</i></b></span><br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Origins</span></i></b></div> <b><i>Parentage</i></b>: Obrimos, Weret-Hekau, Keepers of the Word, Guardians of the Veil (pre-Apocalypse Mysteriorum)<br /> <b><i>Background</i></b>: Pharaoh Djoser's twin Imhotep greatly capitalised on having the best possible education for his time and his later Awakening to the Golden Key, becoming a capable chancellor, head architect and a fourth-degree master. After his death and reinternment in an Aetheric Verge near the Lower Country capital Men-nefer (which vanished during a battle in the New Kingdom period), he became deified and attributed with major contribution to the Black Land's medical arts.<br /> After his death and deification, he became attributed with major developments of Black Land's medicine (though he was only an Adept of Life in life). Accordingly, his disciples and grand-disciples diverged in their magical focus - some kept their attention on Space and Matter, continuing the teaching of the Tamers of Stone and their architectural Attainments, while others delved into the new aspect of Imhotep-as-healer-god, shaping their Akh to become better able to heal patient Asleep and Awake alike. Sometime during the New Kingdom period (probably while dealing with the fallout of the Verge containing Imhotep's tomb collapsing) the Legacy picked up an understanding of Nemesis-as-disease, which made it attractive to the Sepermeru.<br /> At and following the Convocation of Alexandria, the Radiant Physicians' heavy focus on emulating Sleeper medicine meant the Legacy aligned with Keepers of the Word over the Pancrypiates. After the Apocalypse Mysteriorum, the new Mysterium lacked the Keepers' tradition of Exoteric Arete, which means Legacies rooted in Sleeper knowledge first and foremost (like this one) were relegated to historical curiosities, and the Guardians of the Veil desiring to combat the Abyss turned to more specialised Legacies like the Fangs of Mara.<br /> In the modern day, Daimonomica of the the Radiant Physicians are relegated to gathering dust in Athenea and upper levels of Censoria (where they were put in the first place for the sole reason of avoiding offending former Pancrypiates). Maybe a dozen or two Liches have survived the centuries by Patterning themselves into something like Supernal Entities. Any potential recreation by Libertines with medical Techne would have wildly different Yantras (in form, not symbolism - owing to advances in medical knowledge and praxis in the intervening almost 5 millenia), optional Attainments (likely based on psychiatric and/or psychotherapeutic applications of the Mind Arcanum), and have Occult and possibly Weaponry replaced with other Skills (for example Empathy in case of the aforementioned Mind Attainments)<br /> <i><b>Appearances</b></i>:<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Doctrine</span></i></b></div> <b><i>Prerequisites</i></b>: Life 2, Medicine 2, two dots in one of the following Skills: Academics, Occult, Science, Weaponry<br /> <b><i>Initiation</i></b>: The initiate has to nurse by mundane means a Sleeper suffering either a poison or disease of at least Severity 3 or Lethal or Bashing damage equivalent to at least 3L in total (2B being equivalent to 1L - so 3L, 2L2B, 1L4B or 6B) to full health. The process is typically overseen by the initiate's Legacy Mentor, though being an autodidact or learning for a Daimonomicon means the Radiant Physician to be takes this role on herself - cheating by using magic to speed up the process invalidates the initiation, but only Mentors and Daimonomica (or the initiate's Common Sense Merit) explain why.<br /> <b><i>Organisation</i></b>:<br /> <b><i>Theory</i></b>: Healing Arts are the noblest endeavour for Wise to engage in: disease (and to the lesser extent injury and poison) is the direst and most common threat to life. Those who excise them and restore ailing bodies to health are most worthy of praise and post mortem rewards.<br /> Nemesis, too, is a sickness of the world, and to be excised accordingly with heavenly light, so that the world may heal.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Magic</span></i></b></div> <b><i>Ruling Arcanum</i></b>: Life<br /> <b><i>Yantras</i></b>: Applying healing salves (+1), having heavy metal treatments ingested (+2), applying incense to ward off ill air (+1), letting go of patients' excess humours (+2), images (incl. statues and amulets) of deities and saints of healing (+1)<br /> <b><i>Oblations</i></b>: Blessing future medical Sacraments, studying medical treatises, preparing animal, plant and mineral matter for medical application,<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attainments</span></i></b></div> <b><i>1) Banish Poison</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> Cleanse the Body (Advanced Duration)<br /> Optional: Prime 1<br /> Dispel Magic (Advanced Duration)<br /> <b><i>2) Banish Plague</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Life 2, Medicine 3<br /> Purge Illness (Advanced Duration)<br /> Optional: Prime 2<br /> Supernal Vision (Advanced Duration, non-Supernal information) (limited to Supernal and Abyssal information)<br /> <b><i>3) Healing Touch</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Life 3, 2 dots in a second skill from the initiation list<br /> Knit (Instant Casting)<br /> Optional: Prime 3<br /> Aetheric Winds (Instant Casting)<br /> <b><i>4) Lay on Hands</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Life 4, Medicine 4<br /> Mend (Erase scars)<br /> Optional: Prime 4<br /> Platonic Form (Advanced Duration, grants 8-again)<br /> <b><i>5) Divine Restoration</i></b><br /> Prerequisites: Life 5, 2 dots in a third skill from the initiation list<br /> Mend (Instant Casting, Heal Aggravated dmg)<br /> Optional: Prime 5<br /> Ephemeral Enchantment (Instant Casting, Bane)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T08:14:02-07:00","id":1554728,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">So if I understood correctly, their teachings embody the aspect of Imhotep as a healer, curing both physical maladies and the Abyssal sickness that infects the spirit. But I am not sure I understood why they fell out of favor. If Legacies like the </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Choir of Hasmallim</i></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> fight the Abyss physically, and the </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Fangs of Mara</i></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> fight it psychologically, then the Physicians serve the role of combat medics, both ensuring higher team survivability and being able to deal with Abyssal pathogens, so in theory their services would always be in high demand for any Abyss fighting cabals.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T03:02:41-07:00","id":1554890,"title":"","content":"Have you considered making Exoteric Arete a prerequisite? Seems that'd be an easy way to answer why this legacy didn't just jump Orders to one that appreciated them more.","signat